WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:06.600
From secret clues to the Upside Down's origins
to a stack of terrifying horror movie easter

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.309
eggs, the fourth season of Stranger Things
is loaded with things you might have missed.

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:16.040
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and these
are the biggest, best, and creepiest details

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.660
hidden in Season 4.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.039
Spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:24.890
Although Season 4 so far has revealed a lot
of new details, such as One's identity and

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.700
how he ended up as a villain in the Upside
Down, we still don't know exactly where his

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.990
powers originally came from.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.870
But there's a little clue in the final episode
if you turn the subtitles on, because as One

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.350
is using his powers against Two, the captions
read "eldritch power thrumming".

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:45.449
For those who don't know, the word "eldritch"
means something "weird", "sinister" or "ghostly",

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:51.430
and is often applied to describe Lovecraftian
horrors that are ancient, almost unfathomable,

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.750
and from another dimension.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.180
So, this could well imply that, even before
he became Vecna, One's powers originated somewhere

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.640
in the Upside Down.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.199
The Upside Down has probably been around for
thousands of years.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:04.199
Millions.

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.190
I wouldn't be surprised if it predated the
dinosaurs.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:12.070
The subtitles also reveal that eldritch music
plays when Vecna kills Patrick, and that there's

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:17.510
eldritch thrumming when Steve, Nancy and co
find the gate in the Upside Down, and there's

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.550
also eldritch gurgling when they pass through
the gate,

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:25.750
all of which firmly links the concept of this
ancient power or terror together with the

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.890
Stranger Things alternate dimension.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:33.930
Jonathan may be far away from Hawkins in California
this season, but in his room is a poster for

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:39.480
R.E.M.'s debut album Murmur, a clue to the
terror Vecna is wreaking back in his home

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.480
town.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.460
As well as being the band's name, those initials
also stand for Rapid Eye Movement, a phase

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.560
of sleep known for its often vivid dreams
including lucid dreams where the person having

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.340
the dream knows they're dreaming and may even
be able to influence some of the characters,

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.560
story, or setting in their dream.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.370
That's especially fitting for Stranger Things
as several Hawkins' inhabitants are terrorised

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.510
by waking, living nightmares.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:08.229
And it also fits Eleven's story as well, as
she's going through her own type of waking

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.560
nightmare as she relives events from her traumatic
past in the Rainbow Room.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.290
Plus, in the final episode, when One reveals
his origins in his villain's monologue, we

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.420
see a young Henry Creel's rapid eye movement
as he turns back the hands of the clock using

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.990
his powers and when he attacks his mother.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:27.480
And there's even more to that R.E.M.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.480
poster because it shows a field full of kudzu
a fast-growing plant, regarded as invasive

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:38.170
in North America as it kills off surrounding
vegetation, obstructing their access to sunlight.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:43.170
This reminds me of another of the show's horrors:
the vines of the Upside-Down, that amassed

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.840
over Hopper and Will in previous seasons.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.470
The poster's kudzu image also links thematically
to Hopper's season 4 reveal about his time

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.700
in Vietnam where he was in the Chemical Corps
spraying herbicide.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.460
The first episode gives us several early signs
of Max's fate this season.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.640
After awkward talks with her school counsellor
and Lucas, she heads to the bathroom, where

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.110
the image of her staring at herself in the
mirror echoes Will in the Season 1 finale

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:13.580
before he ended up possessed by the Mind Flayer
the following season.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.750
Notice also the graffiti on the walls, with
the words 'see you' next to a pair of eyes,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.970
and further down, the words
'But do you see me?'

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:27.380
Those all-seeing-eyes looking at Max in the
mirror foreshadow her being cursed by Vecna,

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:32.470
and how he spies on his victims from afar,
reaching into their minds without their knowledge

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:37.620
And the words on the wall are also echoed
in Lucas' later apology for not seeing what

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.489
his friend had been going through all along:
I just didn't look hard enough.

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:42.810
But I see you now.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:43.810
I see you.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:48.720
Oh, and there's also a tiger eye poster on
the wall watching during Max and Lucas's argument

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.720
just before she goes in the bathroom.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.870
Vecna's already got a hold of cheerleader
Chrissy, and her retching in the bathroom

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.940
brings to mind Will vomiting up a creature
in the Byers' bathroom in Season 1.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.950
And notice, again, more graffiti of eyes looking
directly at Chrissy in the stall as she's

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.670
haunted by the all-seeing monster.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.099
Also, Chrissy being tormented with visions
of Vecna and sounds of her mother berating

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:16.099
and bullying her is reminiscent of Beverly
being trapped with visions by Pennywise in

00:04:16.099 --> 00:04:19.039
a toilet stall in IT: Chapter 2.

00:04:19.039 --> 00:04:23.680
And the song 'I Was A Teenage Werewolf' that
we hear after Chrissy opens the door, was

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.159
inspired by a 50s horror film of the same
name in which an angry, troubled teen turns

00:04:29.159 --> 00:04:34.749
into a murderous monster after being experimented
on by a doctor with his own agenda, which

00:04:34.749 --> 00:04:38.259
certainly has shades of One's experience with
Dr Brenner.

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:42.400
And that same teenage werewolf movie also
appears in IT.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.199
Similar to the way Pennywise returns to Derry
every 27 years for his killing sprees which

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:52.800
often target children, there's also a 27-year
gap between Henry Creel murdering his family

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:59.830
in 1959 and his return to Hawkins as Vecna
in 1986 when he begins killing teenagers.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:04.699
And when Vecna attacks Patrick, the time is
27 minutes past nine.

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:07.779
My walkie wasn't the only thing that got soaked.

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:08.779
9:27.

00:05:08.779 --> 00:05:13.500
Vecna also puts his victims in a psychic trap,
tormenting them with horrifying visions before

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.550
moving in for the kill, akin to how Pennywise,
one of the Duffer Brothers' inspirations for

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.789
Vecna,
employs the Deadlights to hypnotise a target

00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:27.169
just before killing them and uses psychological
traps to terrify them to make them extra-tasty.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:34.270
Both Vecna and the Dancing Clown also have
their origins in another dimension, and One's

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.919
love of spiders also reminds me of Pennywise's
monstrous spider form.

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:43.279
And if you're enjoying these horror references
so far, hit that like button, I really appreciate

00:05:43.279 --> 00:05:44.279
it.

00:05:44.279 --> 00:05:48.400
Not only do Murray's Russian language talents
prove crucial again this season, but he also

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.599
makes use of a more physical skill.

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:54.360
If things go sideways, I should mention I'm
now a black belt in karate.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:59.289
And while it's funny to see him roughly quoting
a famous Okinawan karate master in the middle

00:05:59.289 --> 00:06:03.009
of fighting smuggler Yuri,
My fingers are like arrows.

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:04.899
My arms, like iron.

00:06:04.899 --> 00:06:07.349
My feet, like spears.

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:11.419
it's even funnier when you realise that Murray's
previous experience of karate:

00:06:11.419 --> 00:06:13.669
I've only sparred with the other students.

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:14.669
How old?

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:18.430
It doesn't go younger than 13.
...has a lot in common with Dwight K. Shrute's

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:23.419
karate classes in The Office.

00:06:23.419 --> 00:06:27.560
The way that Max is framed in this shot at
the video store, with a standee of Freddy

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:32.680
Krueger leering over her shoulder, anticipates
her possession by this season's Nightmare

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:37.790
On Elm Street-inspired big bad, Vecna, who
terrorises teens in living nightmares, similar

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.680
to Krueger.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.000
Max.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.669
And at the psychiatric hospital, there's an
extra-sneaky Nightmare on Elm Street easter

00:06:45.669 --> 00:06:47.369
egg hidden way in the background.

00:06:47.369 --> 00:06:52.530
But just before I get to that, speaking multiple
languages isn't just a great skill for breaking

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.259
people out of foreign prisons,
I'm sorry, have my translation skills been

00:06:56.259 --> 00:06:57.360
letting you down?

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.430
...it's also fantastic for understanding movies
and shows you love on an even deeper level.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.080
Piacere, Girolamo Trombetta.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.599
What does that mean?

