00:07:50.889 --> 00:07:56.039
Now, back at Pennhurst where Nancy and Robin
are about to meet Victor Creel, played by

00:07:56.039 --> 00:08:01.039
Freddy Krueger actor Robert Englund,
there's a sign that prohibits knives, needles,

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:05.979
and razor blades, a cheeky hidden easter egg
to Krueger's iconic bladed glove which was

00:08:05.979 --> 00:08:11.840
originally made using steak knives and which,
in the third film, briefly features needles.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:17.250
While the scene with Victor is all very Silence
of the Lambs, Robert Englund also gives another

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:22.870
nod to his most famous character when he scratches
his nails along the metal table in his cell.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:28.419
The gruesome design of Vecna's enlarged left
hand and its distorted, elongated fingers

00:08:28.419 --> 00:08:34.330
and claws also tips its hat to Krueger's glove
with its long fingernail-like blades.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:38.900
And during Fred's waking nightmare, a vision
of a little girl accuses him with a finger

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:43.120
that grows into a horrifying pointed claw
like one of Vecna's;

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.870
and the shot feels like a twisted, creepy
version of E.T.'s famous point, especially

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.350
given the many other E.T.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.580
easter eggs this season.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:56.010
And there's a sinister little detail when
One attacks using his left hand in contrast

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.030
to Eleven who uses her right hand to exercise
her powers.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:04.590
This is no coincidence as in many cultures
and religions, the left side has often been

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.080
associated with evil and bad luck.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.591
Which is also why Dr Brenner's scars, from
the Demogorgon's attack in season 1, are on

00:09:11.591 --> 00:09:13.580
the left side of his face.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:18.960
The way Max will escape Vecna's clutches is
foreshadowed during Nancy and Robin's visit

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.310
to Pennhurst:
We found that music has a particularly calming

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.930
effect on the broken mind.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:28.810
And on the blackboard, there's a list of records,
all of which have titles related to dreams

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.620
and night-time, appropriately enough given
this season's villain.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:38.080
I'll See You In My Dreams is about an ex-lover
who the singer still loves, while Red Sails

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.500
In The Sunset is sung by someone hoping their
loved one returns.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.980
So both songs fit Nancy's situation with Steve
and Jonathan.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:51.090
And keeping with Season 4's dream theme, in
Suzie's room there's a poster for The Wizard

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:55.330
of Oz, in which Dorothy wakes up to find Oz
was all a dream.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:10:00.110
Also in her room are two posters for The Muppet
Movie, a comedy road-trip film that reveals

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:06.210
the Muppets origin story and, much like Eleven's
origin, rainbows are a big feature as is a

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:09.380
song all about dreams and dreamers.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:13.800
Along with Stephen King and John Carpenter,
Steven Spielberg has been very much part of

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:19.450
the show's DNA since the start, and this season
even the 'friendly mailman' who delivers post

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:24.320
to Joyce looks like an absolute dead ringer
for the blockbuster director!

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:28.761
While I was pretty shocked at first to see
a Spielberg lookalike actor on screen, if

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:33.490
he was going to pop up anywhere this was the
perfect storyline for it as the Duffers have

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.880
said they deliberately channelled his 1982
movie E.T.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.330
for the whole California setting.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:46.100
Also, check out the graffiti when Dustin rings
Steve about subbing in to their D&amp;D game.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.100
E.T.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.460
Phone home.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:53.370
And the score gets very John Williams-esque
especially after the Cali-kids and Mike up

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.760
sticks and head to see Suzie.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.220
Fun fact: the Duffers Brothers' music of choice
to listen to as they wrote the first-ever

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:04.230
episode of Stranger Things was John Williams'
score for E.T.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:09.920
And the Spielbergpalooza continues with super-strong
Indiana Jones And The Temple of Doom vibes

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:14.660
when Joyce and Murray find themselves without
a pilot mid-flight as they soar over snowy

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:15.840
terrain below!

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:20.550
Meanwhile, back in Hawkins, the show's hair
and make-up department channelled Temple of

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.270
Doom's Willie Scott for Karen Wheeler's new
hairstyle.

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:27.020
Plus, there's a Raiders of the Lost Ark cut-out
at the video store.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:31.660
On top of that, there's a major homage to
Jaws when Steve returns from exploring the

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:36.570
new gate in Lovers' Lake and scares the others
in the boat before he's pulled down by a vine.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:42.150
And there's another nod to Jaws via Vecna's
first victim, cheerleader Chrissy, who shares

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:46.400
her name with the first victim in Spielberg's
shark-infested horror.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:51.200
Plus, Chrissy's surname, Cunningham, may well
be a shout-out to Arnie Cunningham, the main

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:56.750
character in John Carpenter's horror film
Christine, based on Stephen King's novel.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:01.350
And the way Chrissy, and the other victims
possessed by Vecna, float up into the air

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.210
has echoes of The Evil Dead.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:08.630
Plus, the way the vines wrap around the victims
also draws on Sam Raimi's film, as did Hopper's

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:11.750
experience with the vines in Season 2.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:16.010
When Dr Owens tells El that she's needed to
win the war against the Upside Down:

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.100
I believe you are our best hope.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.900
Our only hope.
...there's a definite ring of Princess Leia's

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:22.570
message to Obi-Wan Kenobi in A New Hope.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:24.290
Help me, Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.000
You're my only hope.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:30.260
And, in another Star Wars shout-out, Dustin
drops Han Solo's famous

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:33.950
Never tell me the odds
during a game of Dungeon &amp; Dragons.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.760
Never tell me the odds

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:41.370
And although El may mean more to the workers
at the Nina Project than the Queen of Pop

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.370
herself...

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.790
You're bigger than Madonna to them.
...it's actually Hawkins singer Tammy Thompson

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.720
who gets to dress up like the Material Girl.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:51.991
In some ways, Eleven and One are mirror images
of each other.

00:12:51.991 --> 00:12:52.991
We're alike.

00:12:52.991 --> 00:12:55.990
You and I.
And after this season's revelations about

00:12:55.990 --> 00:13:01.840
Henry Creel, we can see how Eleven's experience
of his evil actions sometimes ended up reflected

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.210
in some of her darker moments later on.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:09.060
So, when she twists and breaks the bully Troy's
arm in the first season, it's similar to how

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:12.410
One twists his victims limbs before killing
them.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:17.681
She also snaps a Hawkins lab employee's neck,
like One did to a guard in front of her when

00:13:17.681 --> 00:13:19.130
she was younger.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:23.860
And you can discover even more easter eggs
from Eleven and One's big showdown in my Ending

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.300
Explained video.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.260
Tap the link here or in the video description
below to watch that.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:34.200
So, Movie Lovers, what other details and easter
eggs did you notice in the new season?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.330
Let me know in the comments below.

